# The docs are searchable without ever mixing products

## Story

As the part of the system that has to answer questions,
I want our product docs stored in a way that keeps each product's facts separate and ties every passage back to where it came from,
so that every answer can name its source and we never attribute one product's fact to another.

## What this is

There are two jobs here.

The first is a one-time preparation step: take the company's product docs and
turn them into a searchable local store, then stop. It reports what it did for
each file and doesn't run as part of a live call — the live system only ever
reads what was already prepared. Preparing again is safe: if a usable store is
already there, it can simply confirm that and leave it alone.

The second is the search itself: given a question, hand back the handful of
passages most relevant to it, best match first. Every passage carries its own
text, a clear pointer to where it came from — which document and which section
— and a sense of how close a match it is.

The one mistake this must never make is blurring different products together.
If one part of the docs says one product keeps its data for ninety days,
another for seven, and another indefinitely, those have to stay three separate,
distinguishable facts. Handing back the wrong product's number is the single
failure this system cannot afford.

## What "done" looks like

- Every passage it returns names its source. It never hands back a passage with
  no source — an answer that can't be traced is useless on a live call.
- Results come back most-relevant-first.
- Different products' facts stay distinguishable and are never merged into one
  blended passage.
- If a document is empty or unreadable, preparation quietly skips it, notes
  which file it skipped, and carries on without crashing.
- A blank or nonsensical question, or any internal trouble, simply comes back
  with no results — an empty answer is a safe answer, never a crash.
- For rehearsal and testing offline, there's a practice mode that returns canned
  results without touching the store or the network.
- Every search leaves one short, quiet note in the running log with the question
  and how many passages came back.
